# PROJECT: PRIMEPREP
## A Complete CUET PG Online Test Series and Examination Platform

Act as a senior software architect, full-stack TypeScript developer, PostgreSQL database engineer, payment integration specialist, security engineer, and professional UI/UX designer.

Build a complete, production-oriented, scalable online examination platform named **PrimePrep** for CUET PG preparation.

This is not a simple landing page, static dashboard, or frontend prototype. It must be a real full-stack application with persistent database storage, authentication, role-based authorization, test management, examination functionality, payment processing, and student analytics.

I want clean, understandable, maintainable code that a student developer can understand and extend.

Do not overengineer the application. Prefer straightforward implementations, clear module boundaries, reusable components, and well-documented business logic.

---

# PART 1 — PRODUCT VISION AND BUSINESS MODEL

PrimePrep is a CUET PG preparation platform where students can purchase subject-wise test series and attempt online mock examinations.

The application must support two primary roles:

1. Student
2. Administrator

Students can explore subjects, browse test categories, purchase complete subject test series, attempt eligible tests, and view their results.

Administrators can manage subjects, tests, questions, pricing, purchases, payments, students, and platform analytics.

The business model is subject-wise purchasing.

A student purchases the complete test series of a subject, not individual tests.

For example:

If a student purchases Political Science, all eligible premium tests in Political Science become accessible.

The student does not need to pay separately for Sectional Test 1, Sectional Test 2, Full-Length Test 1, and so on.

However, purchasing Political Science must not unlock Philosophy, Psychology, History, Economics, Geography, or Disaster Management.

The two platform-designated free tests remain accessible without purchasing the associated subject series.

